in 2012 a little-known tv and movie  performer landed the starring role in  the year's most watched global event  this is the queen's stuntman  well good evening with more than seven  years in the planning the eyes of the  world tonight here on london with the  2012 games finally opening  let's get the thoughts of our guests  here tonight sky ceremonial commentator  alastair bruce who's been here my name  is alistair bruce  the london olympics began on friday the  27th of july 2012. any minute we're  going to see the start with the cauldron  lighting and the games can begin and  these games that night i was on the  balcony of the thistle hotel i think it  was called right beside the tower bridge  and it was the most electric evening  and the opening ceremony  right now at the olympic park in  stratford sky news didn't have  permission to be in the amphitheaters  itself so we were watching much of what  was fed out on a screen very much like  everybody was at home we know they've  been rumors about a bond type film  that's been made for the opening  ceremony so we will keep our eyes on  that bridge so suddenly in the whole  performance the cameras take us to  buckingham palace  and james bond went into the building  i had absolutely no idea that this stunt  involving the queen  and the james bond story was going to  take place from the queen to celebrities  and i thought they can't have got a  stunt double that looks that good and  that like the queen  my name's gary connery  i was asked to be the stunt double to  her royal highness queen elizabeth ii  james bond was chaperoning if you like  the queen to the olympics  and the idea being that we arrive by a  helicopter over the stadium  the two of us jump out free fall  momentarily open our parachutes and uh  he delivers her to the opening ceremony  what essentially this was was a stunt by  the queen i mean this was something that  could go spectacularly right  or wrong  for everyone involved  [Music]  i grew up in  bengio which is a small town just  outside hartford in hertfordshire  whenever people ask me how did i become  a stuntman i always give the flippant  answer of i've bunked off school lots  but in the uk there is  a procedure to get on what's known as  the stunt register  it's not for the faint-hearted  i fly wing suits i base jump i kayak i  crash cars i get hit by cars  i get set on fire  i've doubled for gary oldman on the  batman films  john hurt in indiana jones  anything that you see stuntwise on  television  i'm probably in there at some point  [Music]  around october time 2011  i got a phone call from a friend of mine  who is a rigger in the tv and film world  and he said to me gary are you available  to go to  stratford east london for a meeting and  at the time he didn't tell me  what that was  so i arrived at stratford three mills  studios  about half an hour had gone by and there  was a crackle over the radio  dan is on his way to your meeting now  and everybody's sort of suddenly  adjusted themselves  you know shoulders back chest out kind  of thing and i'm thinking to myself  crikey who is this danny  danny boyle walks in the door  he takes one look at me says gary  hello danny what are you doing here  i knew danny from the film the beach the  leonardo dicaprio movie the beach  when danny boyle agreed to direct the  opening ceremony of the london olympics  his plan was to showcase the best of  british culture  pillars of life like the monarchy  the nhs  even james bond the iconic british spy  it was decided that the centerpiece of  the show would take the form of james  bond and the queen who was of course set  to open the olympics anyway  both of whom  would parachute into the stadium from a  helicopter  for this illusion to work  the queen would need to play herself  alongside daniel craig as james bond  in this mini movie both would be seen to  travel from buckingham palace to  stratford via helicopter  this segment would be broadcast to the  world so it was made to look as though  the action was unfolding in real time  but at the same time a second helicopter  carrying stunt doubles for the queen and  james bond would hover out of sight near  the stadium  when it came to the critical moment the  jump itself  the action would cut to the stunt  doubles leaping  into the arena  the whole thing  was top secret  he  asked me whether it was possible  and  i said you know  falling and opening a parachute and  landing that's that's a given that can  be done  but it just depends what else is within  that arena  what essentially this was was a stunt by  the queen  she herself had decided to do this and  she was participating in it along with  an a-list hollywood actor daniel craig  who was basically james bond this figure  of what is known around the world as the  great british character in film  so i was doubling for the queen and mark  sutton was doubling as james bond  we were using base jumping equipment so  it's essentially jumping from static  objects with a parachute  and it's generally much lower altitude  than one would skydive  it's a different sort of equipment set  up  but they are very good and they work  but also human error can pack the  parachute wrong so  it's not like working in tv and film  where generally you can call cut and go  and do it again this was a one-off  one attempt  in front of you know a worldwide  audience to get it right and so that's  where the sort of level of fear and the  focus and the concentration was at its  utmost  a very good evening after more than  seven years in the planning the eyes of  the world here on london tonight the  2012 games finally opened and boy  so we  got into the uh the helicopter at a  bridge  airfield which is just north of the  stadium i guess by maybe  six or seven miles  so obviously when one is doubling  somebody else there's a whole  costume and makeup team that try to make  you look as much like that person as  possible  angela kelly has been a personal  assistant to the queen for some years  and she has  always known precisely how to dress the  queen well and there will have been a  lot of discussion between angela kelly  and ultimately the stunt man who was  gary and you know gary would have had to  spend time with angela and make sure  that what she made for him  mirrored exactly what the queen was  going to be wearing herself in order to  create the illusion and bring it to as  much a sense of reality as possible  so i had the queen's dressmaker she  measured me up to have a dress made that  could also incorporate the straps of the  parachute  so i was wearing flat shoes i think i  had  some tights on looked very good  this peach salmon dress which was  beautiful  a big costume  ring a big diamond  i had one of the queen's personal  handbags apparently so i'm told  i was wearing a wig  and of course my union flag parachute  i was hugely surprised that the queen  had decided to do this and i expect the  queen would have wanted to know what the  risks were to her reputation and profile  [Music]  if  mark and i had decided we can't do this  even to the second  there was a button that they press in  the control room which goes to  another pre-recorded piece to basically  end the sequence  and i don't know what that was  maybe they pre-recorded a helicopter  then banking away and landing  and then the queen gets revealed again  i have no  idea let's get the thoughts of our  guests here tonight sky ceremonial  commentator alastair bruce  sometimes an event can really bring the  whole country together and over 70 days  by passing this very simple  we took off about 40 minutes before we  would do overhead we know there'd been  rumors about a bond type film that's  been made for the opening ceremony so  the flight from the airfield to the  stadium was actually very short  because we weren't that far north of  where the stadium was but they did want  us up  early so that we were ready and in place  and prepared  our jump would time in with that  pre-recorded stuff  so suddenly in the whole performance the  cameras take us to buckingham palace  and we went up the stairs and james bond  went into the building  and then he went into the room and there  she was it was undeniably the queen  this is a pre-record  but it's made to look like it's  happening in real time  from that moment the whole brilliance of  the concept started to grasp us  of course she goes with the corgis  and we only saw her feet going into the  helicopter we didn't know where it was  going  we were hovering outside the stadium  they were playing the  pre-record on the screens within the  stadium  everyone watching to see if the uk can  put on a show to wow the world even  james bond  we could see those screens from in the  helicopter  and then the helicopter took off  and then it passed certain significant  points  on london's skyline  then it went underneath the great  traverse arch of the tower bridge  and this certainly is danny boyle the  film director at work here knowing what  works visually oh definitely and i think  that throughout we got the call a minute  overhead and absolutely everything ramps  up again at that point  it was dark everywhere the lighting was  phenomenal  people they had these paddles that they  held every seat had a sort of lighting  paddle and so they could hold that up  and  you know the computer systems would then  light all those paddles up  it was just phenomenal  so we were at 750 feet  the towers of the stadium are 210 feet  so that gave us  540 feet to jump out  free fall  open our parachutes  spiral a little bit and then get away  from the stadium to then be able to land  just outside the stadium so this was  going to happen we were going to jump  into the opening ceremony of the  olympics  for all of our rehearsals we'd had a  countdown from 10  so that it timed out with the pre-record  and of course this amazing moment when  the door opened and james bond said are  you ready your majesty  i remember turning and saying to mark  we're going  under sort of a gasp of everybody  we could hear um the bond theme tune  being played out  you know  that kicked in  your awarenesses are so heightened you  wouldn't hear  the blades  [Applause]  and they're literally feet above you but  you'd hear the bells on the toes of  fairies dancing 700 feet below  i remember the parachute opening that's  always a good feeling  [Applause]  i remember then spiraling around to my  left and looking back and seeing mark  and we sort of caught one another's eye  and we were screaming at each other it  was great  then it was all about basically clearing  the  sides of the stadium to get out  over  the towers and all of the cables and  lines and everything that was there  and because of the wind direction we had  to approach over the water and then get  to land on quite a narrow bridge  it made much more sense for us to land  outside of the stadium which also meant  then it was easier to reveal the queen  coming into the stadium  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  the best of british  that was tremendous because the rumors  have been flying around here for several  hours that something like that was going  to happen well they always have a list  of when by the time i came out into the  stadium and sat with my wife  essentially it was already over  from a spectacle perspective but then  the athletes were walking around for  them to have their moments too  it's nice to remain anonymous  this for me  fantastic as it was it was still just  another job  the best job i've ever had a hasten to  add but it was another job  for the united kingdom that was one of  the great worldwide events that we were  able to host  and i suppose the palace were delighted  because in the end it went well there  was a risk but the risk was worth taking  because it was worth taking for the  success of the london olympics 2012  danny boyle pulled it off and it led to  a great fortnight of fabulous athletics  and all forms of sport  the queen hasn't  hasn't taken it upon herself to invite  me around for tea and cakes yet but i do  know where she lives so i might go and  knock on her door at some point  [Music]  in 2013 mark sutton who played james  bond's double on the night of the  opening ceremony died following a  parachute stunt accident involving a  wingsuit in switzerland  gary connery continues to work in the  industry  the queen's stuntman was recorded by tom  gillespie writing production and sound  design by rob mulher  for more information go to sky news dot  com forward slash storycast 21.  next time  the so-called year 2000 computer bug has  generated fears that anything from  nuclear missiles to interbank trading  systems could fail when 1999 turns into  the year 2000  [Music]
 

